{
 "comment": "Parity corpus for the audience helper (nexus-sby49.3; reworked in nexus-sby49.4). Each row builds a layout under a tmp dir, picks a payload and the user's settings file (user: null, an object for conexus.json, \"dir\" for a directory in its place, or a raw string), and names the answer of each reader: guard_mode, project_settings, telemetry_enabled, t1_nudge_enabled and advice_blocked. The plugin copy (conexus/hooks/scripts/_audience.py) and the src copy (src/nexus/hooks/_audience.py) must give it. The previous release's plugin copy (git show <tag>:...) knows only the two legacy markers, so on every row that does not set prev_release to false its nexus_repo answer must equal 'the project is strict'. Paths are relative to the tmp dir and use '/'. A file entry is a file, a dir entry a directory, a link entry a symlink (posix only: a row with a link sets posix_only).",
 "markers": [
  ".nexus/dev-process.json",
  "scripts/agent-worktree-preflight.sh"
 ],
 "rows": [
  {
   "id": "plain-repo-no-user-file",
   "layout": [
    {
     "p": "r/.git",
     "k": "dir"
    }
   ],
   "payload": {
    "cwd": "r"
   },
   "expect": {
    "guard_mode": "seatbelt",
    "project": {},
    "telemetry": false,
    "t1_nudge": true,
    "advice_blocked": []
   },
   "user": null
  },
